diff --git a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
index 9588f14e1..83c32c0c4 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md
@@ -107,6 +107,7 @@ The server exposes tools across three modules in `crates/app/src/mcp/` (see `cra
 
 ### 4. Stock & Tool Management (`tools.rs`, `edit.rs`, `body_tools.rs`, #355, #361)
 - `set_stock { "box"?: { "dx", "dy", "dz" }, "cylinder"?: { "diameter", "height" }, "from_model"?: string }`: Define setup stock as a box in mm (centred in XY, z from 0 to `dz`), a cylinder, or a copy of a model's mesh.
+- `fit_stock { "shape"?: "box" | "cylinder", "margin"?: number, "sides"?: [number, number, number, number, number, number] }`: Fit the active setup's stock to its parts, never fixtures (including vises, accessories and plates). `shape` defaults to `"box"`; `"cylinder"` fits a Z cylinder snug about the parts. `margin` is the allowance on every side in mm (default 2). `sides` gives six allowances in mm, ordered [-X, +X, -Y, +Y, -Z, +Z], and replaces `margin` (box only). Keeps the stock's rotation. One undo step through `SetStock`; returns `{ stock }`. Refused by name: no models, only fixtures, negative or non-finite allowances, malformed parameters (including a `sides` array without six finite numbers), an unknown shape, `sides` with a cylinder, or models with no usable extent (#1538).
 - `set_raw_stock_only { "on": boolean }`: For a stock made from a model (`set_stock` `from_model`), say whether that source model is raw stock only - a casting or blank you cut into, not the finished part. Default off: the model is judged like every model. On: the gouge verdict leaves it out. One undo step. Refused by name when there is no stock yet ("set the stock first"), when the stock is not made from a model, or when the source model has no geometry. The mark holds only while the model is still the stock's source and its geometry and placement (position and rotation) are unchanged, so moving or turning the model voids it; otherwise it is ignored and the post says so by name. An operation that machines the model (as its source or in a boundary pick) puts it back in the verdict. If the mark leaves nothing to judge, the post is refused by name.
 - `list_tool_catalog {}`: List built-in tool definitions.
 - `add_tool { "catalog"?: string, "definition"?: object, "name"?: string }`: Add a tool: a copy of a `list_tool_catalog` entry, or a full definition (`get_job`'s tool shape); `name` defaults to the catalog name.
diff --git a/docs/decisions/1552-fit-stock-skill.md b/docs/decisions/1552-fit-stock-skill.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..70d027d68
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/1552-fit-stock-skill.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+## #1552 - Document the fit_stock MCP tool
+
+**Decided:** Add the shipped `fit_stock` tool beside `set_stock` in the MCP skill. Document the schema, defaults, millimetres, side order, parts-only scope, preserved rotation, single undo step, response and named refusals.
+
+**Why:** Agents need the same stock-fit contract the MCP implementation already exposes. The row follows `stock_fit_tools.rs`, its parameter parsers and `stock_fit.rs`.
+
+**Considered and dropped:** No runtime changes or new dependencies are needed. A separate guide would split the tool reference. Keep the process version and #681 merge announcement with the merging session, as the issue requires.
+
+**Validation:** A focused xtask documentation contract pin fails without the row and passes with it. Restoring upstream's skill reproduces the failure. This avoids rebuilding the app for a documentation change.
+
+**Cost to change later:** Edit the row and its documentation contract pin together if the tool contract changes.
diff --git a/xtask/tests/fit_stock_skill.rs b/xtask/tests/fit_stock_skill.rs
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..cad763089
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xtask/tests/fit_stock_skill.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+//! Provenance: repository MCP stock-fit schema and stock-fit refusal rules (#1552).
+
+#[test]
+fn fit_stock_skill_documents_the_tool_contract() {
+    let guide = include_str!("../../.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md");
+    let row = guide
+        .lines()
+        .find(|line| line.starts_with("- `fit_stock {"))
+        .expect("the MCP skill must list fit_stock in its tool reference");
+    for requirement in [
+        "\"shape\"?",
+        "\"box\"",
+        "\"cylinder\"",
+        "\"margin\"?",
+        "\"sides\"?",
+        "default 2",
+        "mm",
+        "[-X, +X, -Y, +Y, -Z, +Z]",
+        "replaces",
+        "box only",
+        "active setup",
+        "parts",
+        "never fixtures",
+        "rotation",
+        "SetStock",
+        "One undo",
+        "Refused by name",
+        "no models",
+        "only fixtures",
+        "negative",
+        "non-finite",
+        "six",
+        "unknown shape",
+        "no usable extent",
+    ] {
+        assert!(
+            row.contains(requirement),
+            "fit_stock row must document {requirement}"
+        );
+    }
+}

